{"name":"Silver City","hex":"#e2e4e9","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Silver City","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A number of places in the United States, including:\nA census-designated place in Tulare County, California.\nA town in Humphreys County, Mississippi.\nA town, the county seat of Grant County, New Mexico. \nA census-designated place in Lyon County, Nevada.","A census-designated place in Tulare County, California."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Silver_City"}],"entries":[{"title":"Silver City, California","blocks":[{"text":"Silver City is a census-designated place (CDP) in the mountainous area of central Tulare County, California, United States. Silver City sits at an elevation of 6,732 feet (2,052 m). It lies 72 km east-northeast of Visalia, within the boundary of Sequoia National Park. The 2010 and 2020 United States censuses reported that Silver City was uninhabited."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Tulare_County_California_Incorporated_and_Unincorporated_areas_Silver_City_Highlighted_0671932.svg/330px-Tulare_County_California_Incorporated_and_Unincorporated_areas_Silver_City_Highlighted_0671932.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver_City%2C_California","wikidata":"Q6128445"},{"title":"Silver City, Georgia","blocks":[{"text":"Silver City is an unincorporated community in Dawson and Forsyth counties, in the U.S. state of Georgia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Chevron%2C_Silver_City_GA.jpg/330px-Chevron%2C_Silver_City_GA.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver_City%2C_Georgia","wikidata":"Q65043833"},{"title":"Silver City (2004 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Silver City is a 2004 American political satire comedy-drama film written and directed by John Sayles. Chris Cooper portrays an inept Republican gubernatorial candidate, a character that was noted for similarities to U.S. President George W. Bush. The film's large ensemble cast includes, among others, Richard Dreyfuss, Danny Huston, Michael Murphy, Maria Bello, Kris Kristofferson, Mary Kay Place, Thora Birch, Tim Roth, Billy Zane and Daryl Hannah."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9f/Silver_City_poster.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver_City_(2004_film)","wikidata":"Q742593"},{"title":"City","blocks":[{"text":"A city is a human settlement of a substantial size. The term \"city\" has different meanings around the world and in some places the settlement can be very small. Even where the term is limited to larger settlements, there is no universally agreed definition of the lower numerical boundary for their size. In a more specific sense, a city can be defined as a permanent and densely populated place with administratively defined boundaries whose members work primarily on non-agricultural tasks. Cities generally have extensive systems for housing, transportation, sanitation, utilities, land use, production of goods, and communication. Their density facilitates interaction between people, government organizations, and businesses, sometimes benefiting different parties in the process, such as improving the efficiency of goods and service distribution."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Tokyo_Shibuya_Scramble_Crossing_2018-10-09.jpg/330px-Tokyo_Shibuya_Scramble_Crossing_2018-10-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/City","wikidata":"Q515"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Lagos-centre-from-executive-lounge-Continental-hotel-2026-IMG_7970_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Lagos-centre-from-executive-lounge-Continental-hotel